# Release Logging Rule

After completing ANY code change (feature, fix, refactor, config change,
dependency bump, etc.), append a new entry to `releases.md` at the TOP of
the file (directly below the `# Releases` header), using this exact format:

## [YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM] Short imperative title of the change

**By:** @cline

**Requested:** One sentence describing what was asked for, in the user's
own intent — not just a restatement of the diff.

**Changes:**
- `path/to/file.ext` — what changed and why. Reference specific
  functions, props, or behavior, not just "updated file".
- `path/to/other-file.ext` — one bullet per file, or per logical
  group of files if several touched the same concern.

**Notes:** Optional. Caveats, edge cases, follow-ups, dead code found, or
decisions the user should know about that aren't obvious from the diff.

## Rules
- Always insert the newest entry at the top of the file (reverse
  chronological order) — never append to the bottom.
- Include both date AND time in the header timestamp, since multiple
  entries can land on the same day.
- Do this for every change, no matter how small — a one-line fix still
  gets an entry.
- Do this automatically as the last step of every task. Do not ask for
  permission and do not skip it.
- If unsure of the current date/time, ask the user rather than guessing.
- Never remove or rewrite older entries in `releases.md` — this file is
  an append-only historical log.
